<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31502" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσπνέω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πνεύσομαι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inhale,</i> opp.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναπνέω, ἐκπνέω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Resp.</u>
				472b3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				887b17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>inhale,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					2.35
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐοσμίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristaenet.
					1.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>breathe upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">με αὔρα τις εἰσέπνευσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					314
				</span></i>
			 (
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέμῳ ἐσπνεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					2.8
				</span></i>
			) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					3.12
				</span></i>
			 (a Lacedaemonian phrase for <i>inspire with love</i>);
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὴν ἀναπνοήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SA</u>
					1.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
